{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"sec-5","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:56af3c7e2758851c18ce1c7cfe419208686d0442345d09615ed71c6050bb11ef/papers/short.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/short?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196","passage_ref":"sha256:a1593370c38e12db1c19bd7e6926ae58ff48cf2267100066f3070a6a2aaeb22c/papers/short.md/sha256:56af3c7e2758851c18ce1c7cfe419208686d0442345d09615ed71c6050bb11ef/papers/short.json/passages/sec-5","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&paper=short&passage=sec-5","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&paper=short&passage=sec-5","span":{"end_byte":158846,"end_line":1177,"start_byte":98138,"start_line":734},"stage":"short"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&view=arguments&node=euler.proposition-5.11&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&node=euler.proposition-5.11&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&node=euler.proposition-5.11&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&view=arguments&node=euler.proposition-5.11&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=1a04095979abc1f47f92053bb15471a69a264fe46468a75d5f115a64df047196&ref=sha256%3Ab6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b%2Fnodes%2Feuler.proposition-5.11","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"A result as the authors number it. Its links to the Lean were made with AI for Proof Reader and have not been reviewed by the authors.","citation_ids":["cite.euler.proposition-5.11"],"evidence_ids":["link.euler.proposition-5.11"],"id":"euler.proposition-5.11","kind":"claim","label":"Proposition 5.11","locator":"Proposition 5.11, Section 5","source_id":"paper","statement":"**Proposition 5.11.** Let $\\Lambda\\ge1$, and with the depth $P$ of the expansion put $$\\begin{equation}\n u=S_\\Lambda V,\\qquad v_\\Lambda=u-V,\\qquad\n \\varepsilon_\\Lambda=\\Lambda^{2-P}\n \\bigl(1+\\left\\lVert V\\right\\rVert_{C_tC^{P,1/2}}\\bigr)^2 . \\tag{5.55}\n\\end{equation}$$ Let $p$ be the function of zero mean with $\\Delta p=-\\operatorname{tr}((\\nabla u)^2)$, and let $R_u=u_t+u\\cdot\\nabla u+\\nabla p$. Then $u$ is smooth, odd, divergence free and supported on frequencies at most $2\\Lambda$, its residual $R_u$ is odd, divergence free and supported on frequencies at most $4\\Lambda$, and $$\\begin{equation}\n \\left\\lVert v_\\Lambda\\right\\rVert_{C_tC^{2,1/2}}\\le C_{2,P}\\varepsilon_\\Lambda,\\qquad\n \\left\\lVert R_u\\right\\rVert_{C_tC^{1,1/2}}+\\left\\lVert D^2(p-\\Pi)\\right\\rVert_{C_tC^{0,1/2}}\n \\le C\\left\\lVert R_V\\right\\rVert_{C_tC^{1,1/2}}+C_{2,P}\\varepsilon_\\Lambda . \\tag{5.56}\n\\end{equation}$$ Moreover, on $[0,T]\\times\\mathbb T^3$, $$\\begin{equation}\n D^2(p-p_U)\\le\\bigl(C_{\\rm step}\\lambda^{-1/4}\n   +C\\left\\lVert R_V\\right\\rVert_{C_tC^{1,1/2}}+C_{2,P}\\varepsilon_\\Lambda\\bigr)\\operatorname{Id}. \\tag{5.57}\n\\end{equation}$$","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.proposition-5.11","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/nodes/euler.proposition-5.11","id":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.proposition-5.11%22%2C%22euler.lemma-5.8%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:b6895856d9ff50e16496b37b717873bb085652575bcb8d1394efc1e2e75b460b/edges/%5B%22euler.proposition-5.11%22%2